---
import '@fontsource-variable/archivo/wdth.css';
import '@fontsource/dm-mono/400.css';
import { identity } from '../data/portfolio-entries';
import { emailHref } from '../data/site-links';
import ContactLinks from '../components/ContactLinks.astro';
import { personSchema, siteUrl } from '../data/seo';

const title = 'Dave Bettner | Customer-facing technical delivery';
const description =
  'Dave Bettner works with customers on the messy part of implementation: turning an unclear workflow into a system people can use and trust. Ten years in reporting, assurance, healthcare, and integration systems, with newer public agent engineering work published for inspection.';
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head>
  <meta charset="utf-8"/>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/>
  <meta name="description" content={description}/>
  <meta name="robots" content="index, follow"/>
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#08090b"/>
  <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark"/>
  <link rel="canonical" href={`${siteUrl}/`}/>
  <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"/>
  <link rel="alternate icon" href="/favicon.ico"/>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/interstellar-system.css"/>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/sphere-gradient.css"/>
  <meta property="og:type" content="profile"/>
  <meta property="og:title" content={title}/>
  <meta property="og:description" content={description}/>
  <meta property="og:url" content={`${siteUrl}/`}/>
  <meta property="og:image" content={`${siteUrl}/images/dave-bettner-og.jpg`}/>
  <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200"/>
  <meta property="og:image:height" content="630"/>
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"/>
  <meta name="twitter:title" content={title}/>
  <meta name="twitter:description" content={description}/>
  <meta name="twitter:image" content={`${siteUrl}/images/dave-bettner-og.jpg`}/>
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(personSchema)}></script>
  <title>{title}</title>
</head><body><a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><div class="wrap masthead"><a class="mast-brand" href="/"><span class="mast-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="mast-name">{identity.name}</span></a><nav class="primary-nav" aria-label="Primary navigation"><a href="/work/">Work</a><a href="/experience/">Experience</a><a href="#contact">Contact</a></nav></div></header><main id="main">
<section id="top" class="cover"><div class="interstellar-field sphere-field" data-interstellar-field data-sphere-gradient aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="wrap cover-grid"><div class="cover-copy"><h1><span>DAVE</span><span>BETTNER</span></h1><p class="role-line">Solutions architecture · implementation leadership · agent systems</p><p class="cover-role">I work with customers on the messy part: turning an unclear workflow into a system people can use and trust.</p><p class="cover-qualifier">I have spent ten years implementing reporting, assurance, healthcare, and integration systems. The agent work is newer. I publish it so you can inspect it.</p><div class="cover-actions"><a class="round blue" href="/work/">View work</a><a class="round ghost" href="/experience/">Read experience</a></div></div><figure class="cover-specimen"><span class="portrait-halftone" data-portrait-backdrop aria-hidden="true"></span><img class="cover-portrait" src="/images/dave-bettner-headshot-20260816-cutout.png" alt="Dave Bettner in a gray suit and navy tie" width="1312" height="1199" loading="eager" data-portrait-source data-source-portrait/></figure></div></section>
<section class="delivery-record"><div class="wrap section-pad"><h2>The work started long before the agent projects.</h2><p class="section-lead">Since 2015, I have led discovery, solution design, integrations, testing, and go-lives. Most of that work has been in reporting, assurance, and other regulated workflows. The public projects show how I am extending that experience into agents.</p><div class="proof-lines"><p><strong>10+ years</strong><span>working directly with customers</span></p><p><strong>Reporting, assurance, healthcare</strong><span>the industries I know best</span></p><p><strong>Public agent and MCP projects</strong><span>new work you can inspect</span></p></div></div></section>
<section class="artifact-flagship"><div class="wrap section-pad"><div class="artifact-grid"><div><h2>The write worked. The response did not.</h2><p>This lab recreates an ugly failure. An agent can write to an internal system. The first write waits for a separate operator grant. Then the API commits the change and fails before it can confirm success. The workflow resumes with the same idempotency key and does not write twice.</p><p class="proof-line">Public CI covers restart and replay, telemetry, a fresh-clone run, and 241 credential-free tests. The cloud configuration is validate-only.</p><a class="text-link" href="/work/hermes-deployment-lab/">Inspect the case →</a></div><figure class="artifact-figure"><a href="/mockup-artifacts/deployment-recovery-receipt.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/mockup-artifacts/deployment-recovery-receipt.svg" alt="Deployment recovery receipt showing operator approval, post-commit fault, and idempotent resume"/><figcaption>A committed write survives a failed response without being sent twice. <span>Open evidence ↗</span></figcaption></a></figure></div></div></section>
<section class="artifact-flagship supporting-case"><div class="wrap section-pad"><div class="artifact-grid"><div><h2>The integration defaults to three guarded tools.</h2><p>Regulated Reporting MCP is a public lab for a Workiva-shaped API. Every write requires confirmation and a readback. If a formula result is uncertain, the tool says so instead of guessing.</p><p class="proof-line">The repository has 126 credential-free tests and 117 registered tool contracts. The full registry stays behind an explicit switch. The offline demo runs without credentials.</p><a class="text-link" href="/work/regulated-reporting-mcp/">Inspect the case →</a></div><div class="case-proof-stack"><div class="case-note" aria-label="Supporting case proof">GUARDED<br/>DEFAULT<br/><span>3 TOOLS</span></div><figure class="artifact-figure"><a href="/mockup-artifacts/regulated-reporting-contract.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/mockup-artifacts/regulated-reporting-contract.svg" alt="Regulated reporting contract showing confirmation, readback, and the guarded three-tool default"/><figcaption>The default exposes three guarded operations; the full registry stays behind a switch. <span>Open evidence ↗</span></figcaption></a></figure></div></div></div></section>
<section class="approach"><div class="wrap section-pad"><h2>I start with one useful workflow.</h2><p>I want one path working before I broaden the scope. I stay with it through testing, failure, acceptance, and handoff. If a change matters, someone should be able to see what happened and reverse it if needed.</p><a class="text-link" href="/fit/">Field approach →</a></div></section>
<section class="evidence-boundary"><div class="wrap"><p>Client work stays private. The public repositories are independent labs and sanitized extracts published in August 2026. They are not client deployments, production tenure, or a Nous affiliation. GitHub dates show when I published the work, not when I first did similar work.</p></div></section>
<section class="cta-block" id="contact"><div class="wrap section-pad"><h2>Have a hard implementation problem?</h2><p>Tell me what the customer is trying to do and where the current process breaks.</p><a class="round blue" href={emailHref}>Email Dave ↗</a></div></section></main><footer><div class="wrap footer-row"><div class="footer-links"><a href="/about/">About</a><ContactLinks/></div></div></footer><script>import '../scripts/sphere-gradient';</script></body></html>
<style is:global>
*{box-sizing:border-box}html{overflow-x:clip}body{margin:0;background:var(--space);color:var(--ink);font-family:'Archivo Variable',Arial,sans-serif;line-height:1.5}a{color:inherit}.site-header{position:sticky;top:0;z-index:50;background:rgba(8,9,11,.96);border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}.masthead{min-height:64px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;align-items:center;gap:28px}.mast-brand{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;min-height:44px;text-decoration:none}.mast-mark{width:10px;height:10px;background:var(--orange);display:inline-block}.primary-nav{justify-self:end;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:24px}.primary-nav a{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;min-height:44px;text-decoration:none;font-size:.75rem;font-weight:650;letter-spacing:.04em}.primary-nav a:hover,.primary-nav a:focus-visible{text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:5px}.cover{position:relative}.cover::after{content:'';position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:1;pointer-events:none;background:linear-gradient(90deg,rgba(8,9,11,.72) 0%,rgba(8,9,11,.46) 42%,transparent 72%)}.cover-copy{position:relative;z-index:3}.role-line{margin:10px 0 14px;color:var(--orange);font:500 .75rem/1.4 'DM Mono',monospace;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase}.cover-specimen{position:relative;z-index:1}.cover-qualifier{max-width:50ch}.delivery-record,.artifact-flagship,.supporting-case,.approach{border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}.delivery-record h2,.artifact-flagship h2,.approach h2{max-width:19ch;line-height:1.06;word-spacing:.08em;letter-spacing:-.025em}.proof-lines{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);border-top:1px solid var(--rule);margin-top:32px}.proof-lines p{padding:18px 18px 0 0;border-right:1px solid var(--rule)}.proof-lines p+ p{padding-left:18px}.proof-lines p:last-child{border:0}.proof-lines strong,.proof-lines span{display:block}.proof-lines span{color:var(--muted);font-size:.9375rem}.artifact-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(280px,.8fr);gap:clamp(24px,6vw,80px);align-items:center}.artifact-grid img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border:1px solid var(--rule);background:#111}.artifact-figure{margin:0}.artifact-figure a{display:block;color:inherit;text-decoration:none}.artifact-figure figcaption{padding:12px 0 0;color:var(--muted);font-size:.9375rem;line-height:1.45}.artifact-figure figcaption span{display:block;margin-top:4px;color:var(--orange);font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:.75rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em}.artifact-grid p{max-width:60ch;margin:18px 0}.proof-line{color:var(--muted);font-size:.9375rem}.case-note{border:1px solid var(--rule);padding:48px 24px;color:var(--orange);font:700 clamp(1.5rem,4vw,3rem)/.95 'DM Mono',monospace;letter-spacing:.05em}.case-note span{color:var(--muted);font-size:.75rem}.approach p:not(.mono){max-width:58ch;margin:18px 0}.evidence-boundary{padding:28px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.75rem;line-height:1.55}.cta-block .mono{color:var(--orange)}.cta-block h2{max-width:16ch;margin:12px 0}.cta-block p:not(.mono){max-width:52ch;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:22px}.cover-portrait{position:relative;z-index:2;max-height:76vh;object-fit:contain;object-position:center bottom}.portrait-halftone{position:absolute;inset:12% 0 0;background:radial-gradient(circle,var(--orange) 0 1px,transparent 1.5px);background-size:8px 8px;opacity:.35}.round{border-radius:0;min-height:44px;display:inline-flex;align-items:center}.mast-cta{display:none}@media(max-width:720px){.cover-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.cover-copy{padding-bottom:0}.cover-specimen{margin-top:-78px!important;max-height:330px;overflow:hidden}.cover-portrait{max-height:300px;width:100%;object-position:center bottom}.proof-lines{grid-template-columns:1fr}.proof-lines p,.proof-lines p+p{padding:14px 0;border-right:0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}.artifact-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.artifact-grid img{order:-1}.wrap{width:calc(100% - 28px)}.primary-nav{gap:8px}.primary-nav a{font-size:.75rem}.cover-role{font-size:1.125rem}.cover-qualifier{font-size:.9375rem}.cover::after{background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(8,9,11,.86) 0%,rgba(8,9,11,.58) 66%,transparent 90%)}.cover-actions .ghost{display:none}.role-line{font-size:.75rem;max-width:34ch}.section-pad{padding-block:48px!important}}@media(max-width:340px){.cover-specimen{margin-top:-112px!important}}
</style>